      "content": "The idea that decline is inevitable is a very heavy narrative to carry, but that path of surrender offers a finality that avoids exploring new possibilities. Even in moments of perceived decay, there is room for new forms of mastery, such as changing your focus from high output to deep connection. Allowing yourself the dignity to pivot or change your definition of \"success\" now is an act of profound self-respect.",
      "source": "target",
